            <div xml:id="d1304">

                <pb facs="1130" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/40</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-14">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1060. Since the report seems to be widely circulated in the United States that
                    the German military authorities in Belgium are stopping food for the needy
                    Belgians, it may seem to you wise to contradict the report. There has been no
                    interference. In appearance, the German military authorities give useful
                    assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
